        "read": false,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "Another quick clarification question...\n\nWhen the heirloom flips and is in play in front of a hero does it become a hero target? My instinct is yes (and this is the way my wife and I played it) but a clarification on this is very important since there are so many &quot;non-hero&quot; and &quot;non-villian&quot; damaging effects in the game. Our logic is that if the hero&#39;s gain benefits from the card it is a hero target and if Kismet gains benefits then it is a villian target. But again, we want to ensure that every victory we have is ligitimate--after all, real heros never cheat!&nbsp; :slightly_smiling_face: ",
